{"title":"This Is a Poem That Heals Fish: An Almost Unbearably Wonderful Picture-Book About How Poetry Works Its Magic","link":"https://www.themarginalian.org/2026/03/21/this-is-a-poem-that-heals-fish/","date":1774109899000,"content":"<h3>“A poem … is when you are in love and have the sky in your mouth.”</h3>\n<hr />\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish.jpg\" /></a><em>“Poetry can break open locked chambers of possibility, restore numbed zones to feeling, recharge desire,”</em> Adrienne Rich wrote in contemplating <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2016/08/23/adrienne-rich-poetry-politics/\">the cultural power of poetry</a>. But what is a poem, really, and what exactly is its use?</p>\n<p>Every once in a while, you stumble upon something so lovely, so unpretentiously beautiful and quietly profound, that you feel like the lungs of your soul have been pumped with a mighty gasp of Alpine air. <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><strong><em>This Is a Poem That Heals Fish</em></strong></a> (<a href=\"http://www.worldcat.org/title/this-is-a-poem-that-heals-fish/oclc/85614782&amp;referer=brief_results\" target=\"_blank\"><em>public library</em></a>) is one such vitalizing gasp of loveliness — a lyrical picture-book that offers a playful and penetrating answer to the question of what a poem is and what it does. And as it does that, it shines a sidewise gleam on the larger question of what we most hunger for in life and how we give shape to those deepest longings. </p>\n<p>Written by the French poet, novelist, and dramatist <strong>Jean-Pierre Simeón</strong>, translated into English by <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/tag/enchanted-lion/\">Enchanted Lion Books</a> founder Claudia Zoe Bedrick (the feat of translation which the Nobel-winning Polish poet <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/tag/wislawa-szymborska/\">Wisława Szymborska</a> had in mind when she spoke of “that rare miracle when a translation stops being a translation and becomes … a second original”), and illustrated by the inimitable <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2015/10/14/louis-i-king-of-the-sheep-olivier-tallec/\">Olivier Tallec</a>, this poetic and philosophical tale follows young Arthur as he tries to salve his beloved red fish Leon’s affliction of boredom. </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish1.jpg?resize=680%2C677&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"677\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish1.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish1.jpg?resize=240%2C239&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish1.jpg?resize=320%2C319&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish1.jpg?resize=768%2C765&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish1.jpg?resize=600%2C598&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish1.jpg?resize=32%2C32&amp;ssl=1 32w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish1.jpg?resize=50%2C50&amp;ssl=1 50w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish1.jpg?resize=64%2C64&amp;ssl=1 64w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish1.jpg?resize=96%2C96&amp;ssl=1 96w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish1.jpg?resize=128%2C128&amp;ssl=1 128w\" /></a></p>\n<blockquote><p>Arthur’s mommy looks at him.<br />\nShe closes her eyes,<br />\nshe opens her eyes…</p>\n<p>Then she smiles:</p>\n<p>— Hurry, give him a poem!</p>\n<p>And she leaves for her tuba lesson.</p></blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish20.jpg?resize=680%2C433&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"433\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish20.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish20.jpg?resize=240%2C153&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish20.jpg?resize=320%2C204&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish20.jpg?resize=768%2C489&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish20.jpg?resize=600%2C382&amp;ssl=1 600w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish2.jpg?resize=680%2C678&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"678\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish2.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish2.jpg?resize=240%2C239&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish2.jpg?resize=320%2C319&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish2.jpg?resize=768%2C766&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish2.jpg?resize=600%2C599&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish2.jpg?resize=32%2C32&amp;ssl=1 32w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish2.jpg?resize=50%2C50&amp;ssl=1 50w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish2.jpg?resize=64%2C64&amp;ssl=1 64w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish2.jpg?resize=96%2C96&amp;ssl=1 96w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish2.jpg?resize=128%2C128&amp;ssl=1 128w\" /></a></p>\n<p>Puzzled and unsure what a poem is, Arthur goes looking in the pantry, only to hear the noodles sigh that there is no poem there. He searches in the closet and under his bed, but the vacuum cleaner and the dust balls have no poem, either. </p>\n<blockquote><p>Determined, Arthur continues his search.<br />\nHe runs to Lolo’s bicycle shop.<br />\nLolo knows everything, laughs all the time, and is always in love.<br />\nHe is repairing a tire and singing.</p></blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish3.jpg?resize=680%2C678&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"678\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish3.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish3.jpg?resize=240%2C239&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish3.jpg?resize=320%2C319&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish3.jpg?resize=768%2C765&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish3.jpg?resize=600%2C598&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish3.jpg?resize=32%2C32&amp;ssl=1 32w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish3.jpg?resize=50%2C50&amp;ssl=1 50w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish3.jpg?resize=64%2C64&amp;ssl=1 64w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish3.jpg?resize=96%2C96&amp;ssl=1 96w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish3.jpg?resize=128%2C128&amp;ssl=1 128w\" /></a></p>\n<p>So begins the wonderful meta-story of how poetry comes into being as a tapestry of images, metaphors, and magpie borrowings. Each person along the way contributes to Arthur’s tapestry a different answer, infused with the singular poetic truth of his or her own life. Lolo offers:</p>\n<blockquote><p>— A poem, Arthur, is when you are in love and have the sky in your mouth.</p>\n<p>— Oh…? Okay.</p></blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish21.jpg?resize=680%2C439&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"439\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish21.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish21.jpg?resize=240%2C155&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish21.jpg?resize=320%2C206&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish21.jpg?resize=768%2C495&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish21.jpg?resize=600%2C387&amp;ssl=1 600w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish4.jpg?resize=680%2C685&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"685\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish4.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish4.jpg?resize=240%2C242&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish4.jpg?resize=320%2C322&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish4.jpg?resize=768%2C774&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish4.jpg?resize=600%2C605&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish4.jpg?resize=32%2C32&amp;ssl=1 32w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish4.jpg?resize=50%2C50&amp;ssl=1 50w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish4.jpg?resize=64%2C64&amp;ssl=1 64w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish4.jpg?resize=96%2C96&amp;ssl=1 96w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish4.jpg?resize=128%2C128&amp;ssl=1 128w\" /></a></p>\n<p>Next, he visits his friend the baker, Mrs. Round, who echoes Thom Gunn’s insistence that <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2016/08/29/thom-gunn-reading-list-academy-of-american-poets/\">“poetry is of many sorts and is all around us,”</a> rather than something reserved for the special formal class of “poets.” </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish5.jpg?resize=680%2C676&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"676\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish5.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish5.jpg?resize=240%2C239&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish5.jpg?resize=320%2C318&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish5.jpg?resize=768%2C764&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish5.jpg?resize=600%2C597&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish5.jpg?resize=32%2C32&amp;ssl=1 32w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish5.jpg?resize=50%2C50&amp;ssl=1 50w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish5.jpg?resize=64%2C64&amp;ssl=1 64w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish5.jpg?resize=96%2C96&amp;ssl=1 96w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish5.jpg?resize=128%2C128&amp;ssl=1 128w\" /></a></p>\n<p>Mrs. Round tells Arthur: </p>\n<blockquote><p>— A poem? I don’t know much about that.<br />\nBut I know one, and it is hot like fresh bread.<br />\nWhen you eat it, a little is always left over.</p>\n<p>— Oh…? Okay.</p></blockquote>\n<p>Arthur turns to his neighbor next, “old Mahmoud who comes from the desert and waters his rhododendrons every morning at 9 o’clock.” </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish6.jpg?resize=680%2C681&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"681\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish6.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish6.jpg?resize=240%2C240&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish6.jpg?resize=320%2C321&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish6.jpg?resize=768%2C769&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish6.jpg?resize=600%2C601&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish6.jpg?resize=32%2C32&amp;ssl=1 32w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish6.jpg?resize=50%2C50&amp;ssl=1 50w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish6.jpg?resize=64%2C64&amp;ssl=1 64w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish6.jpg?resize=96%2C96&amp;ssl=1 96w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish6.jpg?resize=128%2C128&amp;ssl=1 128w\" /></a></p>\n<p>Mahmoud offers his answer with easeful conviction: </p>\n<blockquote><p>— A poem is when you hear the heartbeat of a stone.</p>\n<p>— Oh…? All right.</p></blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish22.jpg?resize=680%2C453&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish22.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish22.jpg?resize=240%2C160&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish22.jpg?resize=320%2C213&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish22.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish22.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish7.jpg?resize=680%2C678&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"678\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish7.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish7.jpg?resize=240%2C239&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish7.jpg?resize=320%2C319&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish7.jpg?resize=768%2C766&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish7.jpg?resize=600%2C599&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish7.jpg?resize=32%2C32&amp;ssl=1 32w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish7.jpg?resize=50%2C50&amp;ssl=1 50w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish7.jpg?resize=64%2C64&amp;ssl=1 64w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish7.jpg?resize=96%2C96&amp;ssl=1 96w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish7.jpg?resize=128%2C128&amp;ssl=1 128w\" /></a></p>\n<p>Arthur hastens home to check on poor Leon, who appears to be asleep, “floating gently amidst the seaweed as if thinking.” And because this is the sort of story in which a canary can only be named after an Ancient Greek comic playwright, Arthur next seeks an answer from his canary named Aristophanes, “who is no bird brain.” </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish8.jpg?resize=680%2C676&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"676\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish8.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish8.jpg?resize=240%2C239&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish8.jpg?resize=320%2C318&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish8.jpg?resize=768%2C764&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish8.jpg?resize=600%2C597&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish8.jpg?resize=32%2C32&amp;ssl=1 32w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish8.jpg?resize=50%2C50&amp;ssl=1 50w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish8.jpg?resize=64%2C64&amp;ssl=1 64w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish8.jpg?resize=96%2C96&amp;ssl=1 96w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish8.jpg?resize=128%2C128&amp;ssl=1 128w\" /></a></p>\n<p>Our imagination is left to ponder why, on the next page, the cage contains not the yellow canary but a red-haired woman, who sings Aristophanes’s answer. Perhaps she is a visual allusion to Aristophanes’s play <em>Assemblywomen</em>, or perhaps she represents a muse, whom Tallec invokes to remind us that the muse hides in many guises and reveals herself in the most improbable of places. </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish23.jpg?resize=680%2C453&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish23.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish23.jpg?resize=240%2C160&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish23.jpg?resize=320%2C213&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish23.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish23.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w\" /></a></p>\n<blockquote><p>— A poem is when words beat their wings.<br />\nIt is a song sung in a cage.</p>\n<p>— Oh…? Okay.</p></blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish9.jpg?resize=680%2C682&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"682\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish9.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish9.jpg?resize=240%2C241&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish9.jpg?resize=320%2C321&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish9.jpg?resize=768%2C771&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish9.jpg?resize=600%2C602&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish9.jpg?resize=32%2C32&amp;ssl=1 32w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish9.jpg?resize=50%2C50&amp;ssl=1 50w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish9.jpg?resize=64%2C64&amp;ssl=1 64w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish9.jpg?resize=96%2C96&amp;ssl=1 96w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish9.jpg?resize=128%2C128&amp;ssl=1 128w\" /></a></p>\n<p>Just then, Arthur’s grandmother arrives and is met with the same question, which she answers after thinking hard, evidenced by the way “she always smiles a silly smile when thinking.”</p>\n<blockquote><p>— When you put your old sweater on backwards or inside out, dear Arthur, you might say that it is new again.<br />\nA poem turns words around, upside down, and — suddenly! — the world is new.</p></blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish24.jpg?resize=680%2C453&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish24.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish24.jpg?resize=240%2C160&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish24.jpg?resize=320%2C213&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish24.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish24.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w\" /></a></p>\n<p>But grandma encourages Arthur to ask his grandfather, too, who “often writes poems … instead of repairing pipes.”</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish10.jpg?resize=680%2C681&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"681\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish10.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish10.jpg?resize=240%2C240&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish10.jpg?resize=320%2C321&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish10.jpg?resize=768%2C769&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish10.jpg?resize=600%2C601&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish10.jpg?resize=32%2C32&amp;ssl=1 32w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish10.jpg?resize=50%2C50&amp;ssl=1 50w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish10.jpg?resize=64%2C64&amp;ssl=1 64w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish10.jpg?resize=96%2C96&amp;ssl=1 96w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish10.jpg?resize=128%2C128&amp;ssl=1 128w\" /></a></p>\n<blockquote><p>— A poem? grandpa says, tugging on his mustache and looking worried. A poem, well… it’s what poets make.</p>\n<p>— Oh…? All right.</p>\n<p>— Even if the poets do not know it themselves!</p></blockquote>\n<p>Frustrated with the multitude of confounding answers, Arthur returns to Leon’s fishbowl only to find him sound asleep beneath his large stone, enveloped in seaweed. </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish25.jpg?resize=680%2C453&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish25.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish25.jpg?resize=240%2C160&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish25.jpg?resize=320%2C213&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish25.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish25.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w\" /></a></p>\n<blockquote><p>— I’m sorry, Leon, I have not found a poem. All I know is this:</p>\n<p><em>A poem<br />\nis when you have the sky in your mouth.<br />\nIt is hot like fresh bread,<br />\nwhen you eat it,<br />\na little is always left over.</em></p>\n<p>A poem<br />\nis when you hear<br />\nthe heartbeat of a stone,<br />\nwhen words beat their wings.<br />\nIt is a song sung in a cage.</p>\n<p>A poem<br />\nis words turned upside down<br />\nand suddenly!<br />\nthe world is new.</p></blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish13.jpg?resize=680%2C682&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"682\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish13.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish13.jpg?resize=240%2C241&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish13.jpg?resize=320%2C321&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish13.jpg?resize=768%2C771&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish13.jpg?resize=600%2C602&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish13.jpg?resize=32%2C32&amp;ssl=1 32w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish13.jpg?resize=50%2C50&amp;ssl=1 50w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish13.jpg?resize=64%2C64&amp;ssl=1 64w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish13.jpg?resize=96%2C96&amp;ssl=1 96w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish13.jpg?resize=128%2C128&amp;ssl=1 128w\" /></a></p>\n<blockquote><p>Leon opens one eye, then the other, and for the first time in his life he speaks.</p>\n<p>— Then I am a poet, Arthur.</p>\n<p>— Oh…?</p></blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish11.jpg?resize=680%2C337&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"337\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish11.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish11.jpg?resize=240%2C119&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish11.jpg?resize=320%2C159&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish11.jpg?resize=768%2C381&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish11.jpg?resize=600%2C298&amp;ssl=1 600w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish26.jpg?resize=680%2C453&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish26.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish26.jpg?resize=240%2C160&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish26.jpg?resize=320%2C213&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish26.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/poem_fish26.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w\" /></a></p>\n<p>Complement the almost unbearably wonderful <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/This-Poem-that-Heals-Fish/dp/1592700675/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><strong><em>This Is a Poem That Heals Fish</em></strong></a>  with other poetic and profound Enchanted Lion treasures: <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2016/03/08/cry-heart-but-never-break/\"><em>Cry, Heart, But Never Break</em></a>, a Danish illustrated meditation on loss and life, <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2016/10/13/what-color-is-the-wind-anne-herbauts/\"><em>What Color Is the Wind?</em></a>, a French serenade to the senses inspired by a blind child, and <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2016/09/12/pinocchio-alessandro-sanna/\"><em>Pinocchio: The Origin Story</em></a>, an Italian inquiry into the grandest questions of existence, then revisit poet Elizabeth Alexander on <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2015/07/29/elizabeth-alexander-ars-poetica-100-i-believe/\">what poetry does for the human spirit</a>.</p>\n<p><em>Illustrations courtesy of Enchanted Lion Books</em></p>\n<hr /><h3>donating = loving</h3><p>For seventeen years, I have been spending hundreds of hours and thousands of dollars each month composing <em>The Marginalian</em> (which <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2021/10/22/brain-pickings-becoming-the-marginalian/\">bore the outgrown name <em>Brain Pickings</em></a> for its first fifteen years). It has remained free and ad-free and alive thanks to patronage from readers. I have no staff, no interns, no assistant — a thoroughly one-woman labor of love that is also my life and my livelihood. If this labor makes your own life more livable in any way, please consider lending a helping hand with a <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\">donation</a>. Your support makes all the difference.</p>\n\n<hr />\n\n<h3>newsletter</h3>\n<p><em>The Marginalian</em> has a free weekly newsletter. It comes out on Sundays and offers the week’s most inspiring reading. Here’s <a href=\"https://mailchi.mp/brainpickings/janna-levin-rebecca-elson-anne-lamott-james-gleick\">what to expect</a>. Like? <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/newsletter/\">Sign up.</a></p>","author":"Maria Popova","siteTitle":"The Marginalian","siteHash":"052ac1be0de11784b9ef27664fbcf33da8263d0e7cb9c6e601ccd959f2d3aa78","entryHash":"918eadfb9e4673c3091dc4267ce4ea5a017d60dd430c6a52ffb7507729841878","category":"Sites"}